seg-0388999448a6 = The CLI (command-line interface) and both bindings funnel through one <c1/> entry point, so they never drift. The packs reuse the shared core (<c2/>, <c3/>, <c4/>); Pack { "4" } (<c5/>) composes the models and estimators of Packs { "1" }–{ "3" } rather than reimplementing them; <c6/> derives a GNSS timeline from geometry that then feeds the Pack { "1" } run. The <c7/> module sits at the signal level between the link budget and the measurement domain: it derives the spectral-separation coefficient <c8/> from the actual signal and jammer power spectra, from which <c9/> now computes its anti-jam <c10/> rather than taking a representative constant (cross-checked in CI (continuous integration)); it also carries the ranging-code (m-sequence/Gold) design-trade.

