seg-7b70e8b1b98a = Every sensor implements the same idea: a stateful object whose <c1/> advances its internal stochastic error and whose accumulated state is read out each tick. Clocks expose accumulated phase; accelerometers expose doubly-integrated position; links expose per-measurement jitter.

# text
# c1: ModelSpec { id, kind, provenance, params }
# c2: provenance
seg-79ab76c6dbc0 = <c1/> travels into the result so every figure in the output is traceable to the published source named in <c2/>.

# text
# c1: HoldoverEstimator
# c2: KalmanClock
# c3: q_wf·T + q_rw·T³/3
seg-514c49659947 = Alongside the analytic <c1/>, the clock pack runs a two-state (phase, frequency) Kalman filter (<c2/>) whose process noise matches the truth model. Coasting through an outage, its phase-error variance grows to exactly <c3/> — the analytic holdover relation — and its online 1-σ bound is used to populate the <b>Integrity</b> figure of merit (fraction of outage samples whose error stays inside the k-σ bound).

